# Store text files with LF in the repository regardless of platform.
#
# Without this, a Windows working tree (where most editors write CRLF) makes
# every touched file show as fully modified: the repository holds LF, the file
# on disk holds CRLF, and each line counts as a change. Text is normalised to
# LF on commit so diffs and reviews stay about content, not line endings.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only scripts keep CRLF so cmd.exe and PowerShell parse them.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch line endings.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.whl binary
*.mp4 binary
*.mkv binary
*.mov binary
*.bin binary
*.pt binary
*.pth binary
*.safetensors binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.db binary
